1
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:32,720
[East 46th]

2
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,840
Table 12 is still waiting on the risotto.

3
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,704
I'm drowning in here,
y'all gotta move, alright?

4
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:00,320
Table 7 wants to know
how much longer for the steak?

5
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,040
When it's ready, you gotta follow the board.

6
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,727
First come, first served, honey.

7
00:02:03,727 --> 00:02:05,528
Garçon!

8
00:02:06,482 --> 00:02:08,277
When did this fish die?

9
00:02:08,277 --> 00:02:12,030
It doesn't smell so fresh. Take it back.

10
00:02:13,792 --> 00:02:14,941
What the hell?

11
00:02:14,941 --> 00:02:16,010
What now?

12
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,602
Table 9.

13
00:02:17,602 --> 00:02:18,613
Again?

14
00:02:18,613 --> 00:02:22,962
Yeah, he said the fish smelled off.

15
00:02:22,962 --> 00:02:24,763
Smelled off?

16
00:02:30,682 --> 00:02:32,402
You fucking kidding me?

17
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:35,242
That fish was swimming an hour ago,
for Christ's sake.

18
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:37,362
What did he want me to do about it?

19
00:02:37,362 --> 00:02:38,906
I don't know.

20
00:02:38,906 --> 00:02:42,448
Should I go shove this very fresh fish
right down his throat?

21
00:02:42,448 --> 00:02:44,210
To swim in his guts?

22
00:02:44,210 --> 00:02:46,162
Oi!

23
00:02:46,162 --> 00:02:49,922
(Open your fucking mouth!)

24
00:02:53,037 --> 00:02:55,172
- We'll see about that.
- Alright.

25
00:02:55,172 --> 00:02:57,522
Hey, there he is, everybody. Table 9!

26
00:02:57,522 --> 00:03:01,042
Our Number 1 fan's right out the door,
just like that.

27
00:03:02,384 --> 00:03:04,185
What an ass!

28
00:03:08,593 --> 00:03:10,394
Oh gosh.

29
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:14,226
What the hell is going on here, pretty boy?

30
00:03:14,226 --> 00:03:16,900
It's Table 9, again.

31
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:18,829
He always finds something to bitch about.

32
00:03:18,829 --> 00:03:20,000
You mean the fine-looking gentleman

33
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,880
with the silver hair, the French nose,
and the Rolex watch,

34
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,602
just walked out the door,
because of your bullshit?

35
00:03:24,602 --> 00:03:25,802
Nah.

36
00:03:25,802 --> 00:03:29,282
He said the fish wasn't fresh.
It's clearly fresh.

37
00:03:32,042 --> 00:03:34,362
The fish ain't fresh, pretty boy.

38
00:03:35,013 --> 00:03:37,802
This is New York City.

39
00:03:37,802 --> 00:03:41,962
You're only here in this position
because of your pretty Asian face.

40
00:03:41,962 --> 00:03:43,210
Let me tell you right now.

41
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:45,989
There's a thousand more just like you,
more qualified,

42
00:03:45,989 --> 00:03:47,536
waiting in line to take your job.

43
00:03:47,536 --> 00:03:49,402
You're off the line, step away.

44
00:03:51,602 --> 00:03:53,102
I cannot risk a bad review

45
00:03:53,102 --> 00:03:56,122
from New York City's
Number 1 restaurant gastronomique.

46
00:03:56,122 --> 00:03:58,066
Whatever.

47
00:03:58,066 --> 00:04:01,202
You can get the bus back to the Bronx, boy.

48
00:04:21,308 --> 00:04:23,548
<i>Boat, you're still up?</i>

49
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:33,488
I've told you so many times
that I don't like being intimate in public.

50
00:04:33,488 --> 00:04:34,479
Why's that?

51
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,522
You're worried
that Eva would find out about this?

52
00:04:36,522 --> 00:04:38,519
When are you going
to tell everybody about us?

53
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:41,416
When will she know
that you're also dating me?

54
00:04:41,416 --> 00:04:42,217
What for?

55
00:04:42,218 --> 00:04:44,930
So she would know
that she got herself a competitor.

56
00:04:44,930 --> 00:04:49,342
I also have my pride.
I won't fight in silence.

57
00:04:49,342 --> 00:04:53,282
Life's more fun with a witch
than a princess, honey.

58
00:04:53,888 --> 00:04:55,802
It's fun being with you.

59
00:04:55,802 --> 00:04:59,682
But we can't make it official.
Why is it so hard to understand?

60
00:04:59,682 --> 00:05:01,658
Should we go on "Chae Show"?
(*meaning to expose)

61
00:05:01,658 --> 00:05:03,762
So we can make it serious and official.

62
00:05:04,947 --> 00:05:07,547
You're not scared of death
while you're there?

63
00:05:08,802 --> 00:05:10,360
Of course, I'm scared.

64
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,902
But I'm more worried
if she doesn't know who I am.

65
00:05:16,712 --> 00:05:18,872
You're screwed man, you know?

66
00:05:18,872 --> 00:05:21,730
That guy's a demon food critic.

67
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:23,133
- What?
- Yeah.

68
00:05:23,133 --> 00:05:25,832
Asshole! Damn it!

69
00:05:25,832 --> 00:05:28,322
How the hell was I supposed to know, dude?

70
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,376
<i>You've worked in four restaurants
in two years.</i>

71
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:37,322
<i>You got fired from all of them.</i>

72
00:05:37,322 --> 00:05:39,115
<i>I couldn't ask any of them
to hire you anymore.</i>

73
00:05:39,115 --> 00:05:40,962
He was messing with me so many times.

74
00:05:40,962 --> 00:05:43,142
Who'd have known that he's a food critic?

75
00:05:43,142 --> 00:05:45,126
<i>If the customer is God,</i>

76
00:05:45,126 --> 00:05:48,194
<i>then the food critic is a father of that God,
remember that.</i>

77
00:05:48,194 --> 00:05:50,498
<i>You are well-known now
after being such a smart mouth.</i>

78
00:05:50,498 --> 00:05:52,922
<i>No good restaurants would hire you from now.</i>

79
00:06:21,168 --> 00:06:22,346
Hello?

80
00:06:22,346 --> 00:06:24,512
<i>What's up, man?</i>

81
00:06:24,512 --> 00:06:26,090
<i>Sorry, I went to bed early last night.</i>

82
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:27,642
<i>Is everything okay?</i>

83
00:06:27,642 --> 00:06:31,368
I think I'll go back to Thailand.

84
00:06:31,368 --> 00:06:34,317
- What do you think?
- <i>I think it's a great idea.</i>

85
00:06:34,317 --> 00:06:35,949
<i>I've told you so many times to come back.</i>

86
00:06:35,949 --> 00:06:37,781
<i>You and I can be on the same team.</i>

87
00:06:37,781 --> 00:06:40,186
<i>You can stay with me.
Food is so easy to find.</i>

88
00:06:40,186 --> 00:06:41,546
<i>Just come back.</i>

89
00:06:41,546 --> 00:06:44,082
<i>You won't starve when you're in Thailand.</i>

90
00:06:46,202 --> 00:06:48,003
Okay, see you.

91
00:07:10,957 --> 00:07:12,397
Yo!

92
00:07:12,397 --> 00:07:15,418
Yo! What's up, man!

93
00:07:15,418 --> 00:07:17,302
I'm here to pick you up.

94
00:07:17,302 --> 00:07:19,562
From where? I came here by myself.

95
00:07:19,562 --> 00:07:21,722
To welcome you home.

96
00:07:21,722 --> 00:07:24,842
Let's go, master. Welcome home.

97
00:07:25,589 --> 00:07:27,984
Hey, you're looking better.

98
00:07:27,984 --> 00:07:30,902
Can you speak Thai?

99
00:07:31,610 --> 00:07:33,210
Let's go.

100
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:51,680
[One Month Later]

101
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:55,722
Welcome back to Pop Star Awards.

102
00:07:55,722 --> 00:08:00,150
We just announced the winners
briefly earlier.

103
00:08:00,150 --> 00:08:02,912
It will be even more exciting this time.

104
00:08:02,912 --> 00:08:08,706
There are many stars, celebs, and influencers
joining us this year.

105
00:08:08,706 --> 00:08:12,789
I'm so jealous of Weechana,

106
00:08:12,789 --> 00:08:14,318
a soon-to-be head of Ruam Thai Chana party.

107
00:08:14,318 --> 00:08:18,066
He's here to support his girlfriend,
Eva Yanin.

108
00:08:18,066 --> 00:08:20,302
Please give him a big round of applause.

109
00:08:21,169 --> 00:08:22,138
Thank you.

110
00:08:22,138 --> 00:08:26,666
Weechai, the owner of entertainment complex,
also joins him.

111
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:29,122
He's here with Pie.

112
00:08:29,122 --> 00:08:33,123
She is one of the breakthrough actresses
of this year.

113
00:08:33,123 --> 00:08:35,562
Please give them a big round of applause.

114
00:08:39,213 --> 00:08:44,034
When we leaked the news
that Weechana will succeed me,

115
00:08:44,034 --> 00:08:46,242
he got a front-row seat.

116
00:08:47,096 --> 00:08:49,184
He's the head of a political party.

117
00:08:49,184 --> 00:08:53,402
If they want to know him,
they need to put an effort in the investment.

118
00:08:55,578 --> 00:08:58,922
Weechai is also benefited from it.

119
00:08:58,922 --> 00:09:02,154
Watch them close, don't let them mess it up.

120
00:09:02,154 --> 00:09:04,634
He knows his job really well, Mom.

121
00:09:04,634 --> 00:09:07,690
He knows that he needs to support Weechana.

122
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:10,208
Siblings from the same parents

123
00:09:10,208 --> 00:09:13,082
can kill each other based on their benefits.

124
00:09:13,082 --> 00:09:16,688
Weechai got his strong stubbornness trait
from his mother.

125
00:09:16,688 --> 00:09:19,162
She is totally different
from Weechana's mother.

126
00:09:20,102 --> 00:09:22,415
You should know this better than anyone.

127
00:09:25,602 --> 00:09:28,002
It's better be safe than sorry.

128
00:09:29,362 --> 00:09:31,042
Yes, Mom.

129
00:09:31,042 --> 00:09:33,843
Now, it is the time
that you all have been waiting for.

130
00:09:33,843 --> 00:09:37,093
It's time to announce
the best series of Pop Star Awards.

131
00:09:37,093 --> 00:09:41,352
Please welcome the two actresses
who will present the award.

132
00:09:41,352 --> 00:09:45,946
The first lady just won
the best actress of the year.

133
00:09:45,946 --> 00:09:49,522
Please welcome Eva Yanin.

134
00:09:52,959 --> 00:09:54,727
And the next lady, please welcome

135
00:09:54,727 --> 00:10:00,525
the winner of our breakthrough actress
of the year award, Ginny Athiya.

136
00:10:00,525 --> 00:10:02,482
So beautiful.

137
00:10:14,101 --> 00:10:15,762
Like a mirror.

138
00:10:15,762 --> 00:10:17,822
I guess it's more like, twins.

139
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:22,072
This is so cool.

140
00:10:22,072 --> 00:10:26,282
Both of your girls got their moments.

141
00:10:26,893 --> 00:10:29,226
What about your girl?

142
00:10:29,226 --> 00:10:32,223
She's not planning to get any moment?

143
00:10:32,223 --> 00:10:37,282
I think that Pie is Grandma's favorite.

144
00:10:37,282 --> 00:10:39,776
And that should be enough.

145
00:10:39,776 --> 00:10:42,997
You should take a good care of her.

146
00:10:42,997 --> 00:10:45,402
It seems like you need to rely on her a lot.

147
00:10:48,488 --> 00:10:51,402
Because you're not Grandma's favorite.

148
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:58,778
It is our great honor

149
00:10:58,778 --> 00:11:02,160
to present the best series of the year award.

150
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:07,482
I got the envelope of the winner
right here, Eva.

151
00:11:07,482 --> 00:11:12,522
And the winner of
the best series of the year goes to...

152
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,720
[The best series award: The Hunter]

153
00:11:21,869 --> 00:11:23,602
Ginny?

154
00:11:23,602 --> 00:11:25,403
Ginny?

155
00:11:30,138 --> 00:11:31,157
Ginny!

156
00:11:31,157 --> 00:11:33,600
Ginny! Ginny!

157
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,784
Eva?

158
00:11:34,784 --> 00:11:36,981
Help! Call an ambulance!

159
00:11:36,981 --> 00:11:38,382
Call an ambulance!

160
00:11:38,382 --> 00:11:40,183
Ginny!

161
00:11:41,682 --> 00:11:44,642
What is going on? Call Weechana.

162
00:11:44,642 --> 00:11:46,187
Got it.

163
00:11:48,101 --> 00:11:51,002
Why are you just standing there?
Call the ambulance!

164
00:11:52,594 --> 00:11:55,080
Ginny! Please help her!

165
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:56,568
Ginny!

166
00:11:56,568 --> 00:11:58,122
Ginny!

167
00:11:58,122 --> 00:12:01,122
Ginny! Please help!

168
00:12:03,242 --> 00:12:05,562
Wake up, honey!

169
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,160
[VIP Room]

170
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:18,605
Hey, how was Ginny?

171
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:20,989
The ambulance came to take her already.

172
00:12:20,989 --> 00:12:23,562
But we still don't know what happened.

173
00:12:24,362 --> 00:12:27,002
I think you need to go to the police station
for interrogation.

174
00:12:32,090 --> 00:12:33,891
How are you feeling?

175
00:12:34,605 --> 00:12:36,173
I'm fine.

176
00:12:36,173 --> 00:12:40,402
She said that I needed to go
to the police station for interrogation.

177
00:12:44,046 --> 00:12:45,797
Don't worry.

178
00:12:45,797 --> 00:12:50,402
It's normal for the police
to ask everyone at the scene.

179
00:12:52,784 --> 00:12:56,682
Do you know what happened to Ginny?

180
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:02,234
I asked someone to call the hospital.

181
00:13:03,144 --> 00:13:05,405
They said
that it could be a severe allergic reaction.

182
00:13:05,405 --> 00:13:06,984
Allergy?

183
00:13:06,984 --> 00:13:08,088
What allergy?

184
00:13:08,088 --> 00:13:10,904
Why did she spill blood like that?

185
00:13:11,544 --> 00:13:14,778
It could be from drugs or food.

186
00:13:14,778 --> 00:13:17,002
I think we should wait
for the result to come out.

187
00:13:18,549 --> 00:13:20,722
I heard that her condition is severe.

188
00:13:28,325 --> 00:13:32,402
Do you think that Eva needs to go
for an interrogation tonight?

189
00:13:36,042 --> 00:13:38,276
I don't think so.

190
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:41,034
Eva doesn't have any personal issue with her.

191
00:13:41,034 --> 00:13:45,114
We all saw what happened on the stage.

192
00:13:45,114 --> 00:13:49,552
Also, the police needs
to question many people,

193
00:13:49,552 --> 00:13:52,837
including the crew members,
the catering team, and more.

194
00:13:53,701 --> 00:13:55,640
Most importantly, I told the police

195
00:13:55,640 --> 00:14:00,120
that I need to attend
a significant press conference tomorrow,

196
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,922
and that you need to join me.

197
00:14:10,137 --> 00:14:12,155
Can you still join me?

198
00:14:13,128 --> 00:14:15,173
Sure, I can.

199
00:14:15,173 --> 00:14:18,562
I promised your dad and your grandma.

200
00:14:19,221 --> 00:14:20,772
You're the best.

201
00:14:23,389 --> 00:14:25,642
I think we should go back home to rest.

202
00:14:26,416 --> 00:14:28,602
Don't dwell on it, okay?

203
00:14:56,344 --> 00:14:58,145
Hey.

204
00:15:00,616 --> 00:15:04,130
You want something sweet?
You can have it today.

205
00:15:05,069 --> 00:15:06,549
It's haunted, isn't it?

206
00:15:06,549 --> 00:15:07,920
Sure, it is.

207
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:10,721
Who wouldn't after seeing it
up close like that?

208
00:15:11,328 --> 00:15:14,960
Do you think it was an accident?

209
00:15:15,754 --> 00:15:18,629
We all know that Ginny is a party girl.

210
00:15:18,629 --> 00:15:23,066
We don't know what type of chemical
runs in her blood.

211
00:15:23,066 --> 00:15:25,194
You mean drugs?

212
00:15:25,194 --> 00:15:29,354
If that's the case,
her agency would have covered it up.

213
00:15:29,354 --> 00:15:32,902
The reporters sent me a text
that she is still in ICU.

214
00:15:35,362 --> 00:15:36,639
Do you think

215
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:39,239
the reporters would see
that it could be related

216
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,799
to me and Ginny auditioning
for the same movie?

217
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,563
About what?

218
00:15:44,205 --> 00:15:46,522
You're the cause of her sickness?

219
00:15:46,522 --> 00:15:49,352
Nope, I don't think so.

220
00:15:49,352 --> 00:15:51,062
Only people from the inner circle

221
00:15:51,062 --> 00:15:54,502
know that you and Ginny auditioned
for that movie.

222
00:15:55,730 --> 00:15:58,914
If Ginny couldn't make it
and you got the role,

223
00:15:58,914 --> 00:16:02,842
it could be a drama
that there was no competitor against you.

224
00:16:04,354 --> 00:16:06,168
I don't want that.

225
00:16:06,168 --> 00:16:09,521
I still wish that Ginny is getting better.

226
00:16:09,521 --> 00:16:11,884
I don't want to see her like that.

227
00:16:11,884 --> 00:16:13,502
I need people to accept me for my talent,

228
00:16:13,502 --> 00:16:15,642
that I am actually better than Ginny,

229
00:16:15,642 --> 00:16:18,019
not because of her accident like this.

230
00:16:20,381 --> 00:16:22,416
Hey!

231
00:16:22,416 --> 00:16:24,741
Why are you pushing yourself too hard?

232
00:16:24,741 --> 00:16:27,573
You're already the Number 1.

233
00:16:27,573 --> 00:16:30,642
It's not for everybody and you know it.

234
00:16:32,813 --> 00:16:34,642
Hey.

235
00:16:35,402 --> 00:16:37,314
Girl.

236
00:16:37,314 --> 00:16:40,522
Are you sure
that you can handle Wee's family?

237
00:16:46,121 --> 00:16:47,922
Actually...

238
00:16:48,949 --> 00:16:51,368
I feel awkward around them.

239
00:16:51,368 --> 00:16:53,826
I've dated him for two years,

240
00:16:53,826 --> 00:16:57,202
and his grandma still can't look
at me directly.

241
00:16:58,077 --> 00:17:01,962
I don't know if I can handle it tomorrow,
but I'm a fighter.

242
00:17:03,542 --> 00:17:05,402
I want to be with him.

243
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:08,531
He's cute.

244
00:17:09,794 --> 00:17:12,456
He is bossy and nags at me sometimes,

245
00:17:12,456 --> 00:17:13,645
and he's too focused on his work.

246
00:17:13,645 --> 00:17:16,602
But overall, he's a nice guy.

247
00:17:17,591 --> 00:17:18,480
Right.

248
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,320
I really wish

249
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:24,162
that the Queen of his house
will adore you soon.

250
00:17:24,805 --> 00:17:27,472
Hey, think about it.

251
00:17:27,472 --> 00:17:30,272
If I'm booked for the project,

252
00:17:30,272 --> 00:17:33,302
I will be a Hollywood star.

253
00:17:34,202 --> 00:17:38,234
I will be a better girlfriend for him
in his family's eyes.

254
00:17:38,234 --> 00:17:40,602
I want to make Wee proud.

255
00:17:41,653 --> 00:17:44,021
Jeez! Your love is so disgusting.

256
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:47,882
It is so annoying, super annoying.

257
00:17:47,882 --> 00:17:50,322
I will rate you five stars
for being so annoyingly in love.

258
00:17:50,322 --> 00:17:53,322
I can't take it anymore.

259
00:17:55,019 --> 00:17:56,820
You're overreacting.

260
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,416
Eva did a really great job tonight.

261
00:18:01,416 --> 00:18:07,942
She was tough
and she didn't yell or lose control.

262
00:18:08,808 --> 00:18:11,402
I was just thinking about this.

263
00:18:12,096 --> 00:18:18,362
You can see people's true colors
when they are in shocking situations.

264
00:18:19,744 --> 00:18:21,568
Does it mean

265
00:18:21,568 --> 00:18:25,248
that you're starting
to like this soon-to-be granddaughter-in-law?

266
00:18:25,248 --> 00:18:27,049
Not yet.

267
00:18:28,608 --> 00:18:31,096
She should have been born in a better family.

268
00:18:31,096 --> 00:18:32,571
Honestly,

269
00:18:32,571 --> 00:18:35,037
if she were born as a daughter
of doctors or government officers,

270
00:18:35,037 --> 00:18:38,733
I could overlook the fact.

271
00:18:38,733 --> 00:18:40,842
But look at her.

272
00:18:42,016 --> 00:18:44,960
She's from the family of
a street food vendor.

273
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:49,202
If she is married into our family,

274
00:18:50,285 --> 00:18:54,162
I will be seated next to a vendor.

275
00:18:57,405 --> 00:18:58,776
Right,

276
00:18:58,776 --> 00:19:01,421
you need to send an invitation card
to Mr. Supoj and his daughter

277
00:19:01,421 --> 00:19:04,258
to attend Weechana's press conference.

278
00:19:04,258 --> 00:19:07,906
I want them to meet Weechana.

279
00:19:07,906 --> 00:19:09,707
Yes, Mom.

280
00:19:14,776 --> 00:19:19,409
<i>There was an incident on stage
of a national award ceremony</i>

281
00:19:19,409 --> 00:19:22,248
<i>that was shocking the whole nation.</i>

282
00:19:22,248 --> 00:19:25,882
<i>A young actress named Ginny Athiya
fell to the floor and was bleeding</i>

283
00:19:25,882 --> 00:19:27,832
<i>before she was sent to a hospital.</i>

284
00:19:27,832 --> 00:19:34,704
<i>The hospital reported this early morning
that she has passed away.</i>

285
00:19:34,704 --> 00:19:37,705
We're sending heartfelt condolences
to her family and fans.

286
00:19:37,705 --> 00:19:39,062
What?

287
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:44,080
[Shocking news! Ginny Athiya has passed away]

288
00:19:45,114 --> 00:19:46,454
She looks familiar.

289
00:19:46,454 --> 00:19:49,430
Sure, she was a star.

290
00:19:52,531 --> 00:19:55,576
Hey! Look, look!

291
00:19:55,576 --> 00:19:59,592
I will be having a job interview with her.
This Eva Yanin.

292
00:19:59,592 --> 00:20:02,040
A job interview?

293
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,682
You have to be that formal?

294
00:20:03,682 --> 00:20:04,979
Her manager said

295
00:20:04,979 --> 00:20:08,024
that she is looking for a personal trainer
who can sculpt her body.

296
00:20:08,024 --> 00:20:10,350
She needs to build up beautiful muscles,
increase her strength,

297
00:20:10,350 --> 00:20:12,728
and flexibility for her new action role.

298
00:20:12,728 --> 00:20:14,344
The manager also said

299
00:20:14,344 --> 00:20:17,181
that I could have a chance
to work with a stunt coordinator.

300
00:20:17,181 --> 00:20:19,181
It's Hollywood action movie.

301
00:20:19,181 --> 00:20:20,382
Okay, okay.

302
00:20:20,382 --> 00:20:22,925
I really want this job, man.

303
00:20:22,925 --> 00:20:27,562
I freaking want this job! I want it!

304
00:20:28,498 --> 00:20:32,290
But I don't know how I can compete
with other famous personal trainers.

305
00:20:32,290 --> 00:20:34,440
Of course, you can do it.

306
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,114
But I don't get it.

307
00:20:36,114 --> 00:20:39,730
Why didn't she just hire a personal trainer
based on their profile?

308
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:41,731
Why does she need to interview them first?

309
00:20:41,731 --> 00:20:44,077
For TikTok content, my friend.

310
00:20:44,077 --> 00:20:45,079
She's famous.

311
00:20:45,079 --> 00:20:47,170
Everything she does needs to be documented

312
00:20:47,170 --> 00:20:49,229
for content, for her events and so on.

313
00:20:49,229 --> 00:20:51,928
She's the most famous actress in Thailand,

314
00:20:51,928 --> 00:20:54,520
and her boyfriend is a politician's son.

315
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:57,162
- So privileged.
- Yeah.

316
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:26,504
Pun.

317
00:21:26,504 --> 00:21:27,544
What?

318
00:21:27,544 --> 00:21:31,432
If we get this job,
I think we will live a comfortable life.

319
00:21:31,432 --> 00:21:33,800
We can be on the celebs' list,

320
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:36,429
with good money, and lots of work for sure.

321
00:21:36,429 --> 00:21:38,322
Wait.

322
00:21:38,322 --> 00:21:40,123
What do you mean by "we"?

323
00:21:42,045 --> 00:21:44,552
You can be in my team.

324
00:21:44,552 --> 00:21:45,960
No!

325
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,762
I came back to open a restaurant.

326
00:21:52,006 --> 00:21:54,483
But I can cook healthy food.

327
00:21:56,589 --> 00:21:57,965
Genius!

328
00:21:57,965 --> 00:22:00,624
You're so genius!

329
00:22:00,624 --> 00:22:04,122
- We can work together.
- That's right, my man.

330
00:22:04,122 --> 00:22:06,618
You can make us charge for more.

331
00:22:06,618 --> 00:22:09,642
Listen to me, I can be a personal trainer,

332
00:22:09,642 --> 00:22:11,932
and you're a chef who graduated
from sports science from overseas,

333
00:22:11,932 --> 00:22:13,880
who can work as their nutritionist.

334
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:16,813
Fuck! I love this idea.

335
00:22:16,813 --> 00:22:20,122
It's not bad, not bad at all.

336
00:22:20,122 --> 00:22:23,328
We will gain more than
what we usually make, times two.

337
00:22:23,328 --> 00:22:25,070
Even higher than that
for three to four months.

338
00:22:25,070 --> 00:22:26,871
How much money are we talking about?

339
00:22:30,322 --> 00:22:32,360
- I think it's over a hundred thousand...
- What?

340
00:22:32,360 --> 00:22:34,061
- Per month...
- Damn!

341
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:36,365
- Per person.
- Oh my!

342
00:22:36,365 --> 00:22:38,842
- Count me in, Coach!
- What are we waiting for, Chef!

343
00:22:38,842 --> 00:22:41,138
- Yeah!
- I'm in!

344
00:22:41,842 --> 00:22:43,304
We're gonna make money.

345
00:22:43,304 --> 00:22:46,099
Lots of money!

346
00:22:46,962 --> 00:22:49,122
Hurry up and plan. Come, let's go.

347
00:22:49,122 --> 00:22:51,502
When can I get an autopsy report?

348
00:22:54,650 --> 00:22:56,277
Good.

349
00:22:56,277 --> 00:23:00,042
Send it to me confidentially.

350
00:23:01,725 --> 00:23:03,115
Good.

351
00:23:30,453 --> 00:23:32,254
Just a second.

352
00:23:39,968 --> 00:23:42,922
- Hello, Weechana.
- Morning.

353
00:23:46,093 --> 00:23:48,082
How is Eva?

354
00:23:48,082 --> 00:23:49,576
She heard the news, right?

355
00:23:49,576 --> 00:23:52,402
Yeah, it was shocking for her.

356
00:23:59,853 --> 00:24:01,283
Wee?

357
00:24:01,283 --> 00:24:03,084
How are you feeling?

358
00:24:06,959 --> 00:24:10,458
It's okay, you've done your best.

359
00:24:10,458 --> 00:24:11,719
Right.

360
00:24:14,192 --> 00:24:16,149
Can you go out today?

361
00:24:16,149 --> 00:24:20,202
If you can't, I can call and tell my dad
that you want to rest.

362
00:24:21,136 --> 00:24:22,877
It's okay. I can make it.

363
00:24:22,877 --> 00:24:24,722
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

364
00:24:25,501 --> 00:24:27,322
You're the best.

365
00:24:28,504 --> 00:24:30,922
- We should get going.
- Let's go.

366
00:24:31,805 --> 00:24:34,162
If it's too much for you, let me know.

367
00:24:35,181 --> 00:24:36,525
I can do it.

368
00:24:36,525 --> 00:24:38,682
- Sure?
- I'm sure.

369
00:24:42,045 --> 00:24:44,602
Keep your head up, Eva.

370
00:24:46,482 --> 00:24:48,682
- See you later, Wee.
- See you later.

371
00:24:49,522 --> 00:24:52,762
Please wear marigold garland next time.

372
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:58,640
[Ruam Thai Chana Party]

373
00:25:11,683 --> 00:25:13,722
What is your opinion on Ginny's tragedy?

374
00:25:13,722 --> 00:25:14,440
People said

375
00:25:14,440 --> 00:25:17,320
that you should have tried harder
to save Ginny.

376
00:25:17,320 --> 00:25:18,537
What do you think?

377
00:25:18,537 --> 00:25:20,302
I'm sorry, excuse me.

378
00:25:20,302 --> 00:25:22,962
We should save these questions for later.

379
00:25:22,962 --> 00:25:27,160
Eva is upset about the incident,
and it caught her off guard.

380
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:30,461
Besides, this is a press conference
about my party.

381
00:25:30,461 --> 00:25:33,862
We need to go inside right now,
it's about to start.

382
00:25:33,862 --> 00:25:34,963
We'll see you all inside.

383
00:25:34,963 --> 00:25:36,764
Excuse us.

384
00:25:46,502 --> 00:25:48,303
Good morning.

385
00:25:48,978 --> 00:25:50,779
Hello.

386
00:25:54,852 --> 00:25:56,621
Eva.

387
00:25:56,621 --> 00:25:59,277
I'm sorry about last night.

388
00:25:59,277 --> 00:26:02,109
And thank you for coming.

389
00:26:02,109 --> 00:26:06,682
It's your and Wee's important day.
I need to come no matter what.

390
00:26:06,682 --> 00:26:08,997
Nice and stable, that's great.

391
00:26:08,997 --> 00:26:12,405
If you want to be a part of this family,
you gotta be strong.

392
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:15,302
Let me know if you need my help.

393
00:26:15,302 --> 00:26:16,563
Okay.

394
00:26:17,560 --> 00:26:20,002
Pie, Grandma is looking for you.

395
00:26:20,002 --> 00:26:21,902
Okay.

396
00:26:26,512 --> 00:26:30,469
You got a huge moment last night, Eva.

397
00:26:30,469 --> 00:26:32,670
Your value has suddenly been elevated.

398
00:26:35,240 --> 00:26:38,450
I don't think anybody
would want this kind of moment.

399
00:26:38,450 --> 00:26:40,280
Oh my goodness,

400
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:44,762
did I just say what was on my mind out loud?

401
00:26:56,776 --> 00:26:58,577
Come here, honey.

402
00:26:59,442 --> 00:27:00,952
Thank you so much

403
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:02,480
- for helping out with the event.
- You're welcome.

404
00:27:02,480 --> 00:27:05,352
You are lighting up the event.

405
00:27:05,352 --> 00:27:08,728
Eva also helped to bring in
so many reporters.

406
00:27:08,728 --> 00:27:12,109
Chai, you should go out
and welcome the guests.

407
00:27:12,109 --> 00:27:15,634
You can leave Pie here with me, okay?

408
00:27:15,634 --> 00:27:18,941
Wee, you also need to prepare for the event.

409
00:27:18,941 --> 00:27:21,142
Please take care of Supoj.

410
00:27:21,142 --> 00:27:23,117
I heard
that he brought his daughter with him.

411
00:27:23,117 --> 00:27:25,480
She just graduated from Boston.

412
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:28,020
I think it's the same college as yours.

413
00:27:28,020 --> 00:27:30,656
She's a pretty lady. Do you know her, Pie?

414
00:27:30,656 --> 00:27:33,200
I do, Grandma. Her name is Nicole.

415
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:35,050
She's so popular.

416
00:27:35,050 --> 00:27:36,768
She's pretty and talented.

417
00:27:36,768 --> 00:27:41,162
I heard she had her own fashion brand
even before she graduated.

418
00:27:51,632 --> 00:27:55,749
Today is a special day for Ruam Thai Chana.

419
00:27:55,749 --> 00:27:58,840
I have been a leader of this party
for such a long time.

420
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:02,909
I've seen younger generation's talent
and their determination

421
00:28:02,909 --> 00:28:05,702
and they can continue the party's principles,

422
00:28:05,702 --> 00:28:07,503
like Weechana.

423
00:28:08,656 --> 00:28:13,725
I will continue my contribution to the party
as its advisor

424
00:28:13,725 --> 00:28:16,262
and I will provide my full support.

425
00:28:16,262 --> 00:28:21,482
Please allow my son
a chance to prove himself.

426
00:28:30,413 --> 00:28:33,458
Thank you, thank you so much.

427
00:28:33,458 --> 00:28:36,637
I'd like to humbly accept this opportunity.

428
00:28:36,637 --> 00:28:40,096
I promise
that I will continue the party's policies

429
00:28:40,096 --> 00:28:43,184
that have started with my great effort.

430
00:28:43,184 --> 00:28:47,464
I want to be a small part
in developing this country.

431
00:28:47,464 --> 00:28:49,265
Thank you.

432
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:08,400
Congratulations, I knew you would get it.

433
00:29:08,400 --> 00:29:10,201
Thank you.

434
00:29:21,072 --> 00:29:23,882
You don't have a bouquet for him?

435
00:29:24,709 --> 00:29:28,402
Nobody would accuse you of being a mute
if you stayed quiet.

436
00:29:46,962 --> 00:29:48,322
Thank you very much for coming today.

437
00:29:48,322 --> 00:29:50,338
Hope the flight was pleasant.

438
00:29:50,338 --> 00:29:52,202
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

439
00:29:52,202 --> 00:29:53,506
Okay, thank you guys.

440
00:29:53,506 --> 00:29:55,402
Please be seated.

441
00:29:56,200 --> 00:29:57,282
Thank you.

442
00:29:57,282 --> 00:29:58,578
- Hey, Wee.
- Hey.

443
00:29:58,578 --> 00:30:00,272
Congratulations again.

444
00:30:00,272 --> 00:30:02,682
- Thank you.
- I know you would get it.

445
00:30:02,682 --> 00:30:06,746
Thank you so much for the flowers,
they are beautiful.

446
00:30:06,746 --> 00:30:10,322
And you were more confident than I was,
so thank you again.

447
00:30:12,514 --> 00:30:15,794
Eva, this is Nicole. Nicole, Eva.

448
00:30:15,794 --> 00:30:17,509
She's my super girlfriend.

449
00:30:18,930 --> 00:30:20,642
Nice to meet you.

450
00:30:22,581 --> 00:30:25,562
I'm so glad the universe made this happen.

451
00:30:26,522 --> 00:30:29,488
I have never actually seen
any of your films though.

452
00:30:29,488 --> 00:30:31,484
But I've heard things.

453
00:30:33,021 --> 00:30:34,962
You were great.

454
00:30:35,693 --> 00:30:39,489
I'll make sure not to miss the next one,
if I have time.

455
00:30:42,168 --> 00:30:43,462
Wait,

456
00:30:43,462 --> 00:30:46,744
We're all in the same room again,
it feels like...

457
00:30:46,744 --> 00:30:48,989
Boston was yesterday.

458
00:30:48,989 --> 00:30:51,522
Yeah, so what's up with you next?

459
00:30:51,522 --> 00:30:53,810
Finally, I'm launching my bag brand
in Thailand.

460
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:55,868
Oh my gosh, that is so you.

461
00:30:55,868 --> 00:30:58,568
Wait, wait, Nicole. Sorry to interrupt.

462
00:30:58,568 --> 00:31:03,882
But do you remember that sketchy bistro,
right next to BC?

463
00:31:03,882 --> 00:31:05,269
Does it still exist?

464
00:31:05,269 --> 00:31:06,682
Yeah, it does somehow.

465
00:31:06,682 --> 00:31:09,184
They renovated a bit, tried to look fancy.

466
00:31:09,184 --> 00:31:11,757
- Oh, wow.
- But, it's still the same place.

467
00:31:11,757 --> 00:31:14,573
Oh, sadly, your favorite dish is gone though.

468
00:31:14,573 --> 00:31:17,762
Wait, my favorite dish is gone? Why is that?

469
00:31:17,762 --> 00:31:20,042
That's horrible.

470
00:31:22,122 --> 00:31:24,050
Nicole just told me

471
00:31:24,050 --> 00:31:26,722
that my favorite restaurant
didn't serve my favorite dish anymore,

472
00:31:26,722 --> 00:31:28,477
the one I told you about.

473
00:31:28,477 --> 00:31:30,278
That's too bad.

474
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:37,502
Yeah. Excuse me, I need to use the washroom.

475
00:31:57,546 --> 00:32:00,037
Are you sure? Can I give you a ride?

476
00:32:00,037 --> 00:32:01,424
It's fine.

477
00:32:01,424 --> 00:32:03,802
It's your big event, you need to stay.

478
00:32:03,802 --> 00:32:05,866
I'm sorry that I can't stay.

479
00:32:05,866 --> 00:32:07,173
I'm tired.

480
00:32:07,173 --> 00:32:10,842
I need to interview
my personal trainers tomorrow.

481
00:32:10,842 --> 00:32:12,432
Hey.

482
00:32:12,432 --> 00:32:14,890
Thank you so much for coming.

483
00:32:14,890 --> 00:32:18,666
People were so excited to see you.

484
00:32:18,666 --> 00:32:21,922
It's your event,
I need to be right there with you.

485
00:32:22,541 --> 00:32:26,573
Congratulations, you were doing great today.

486
00:32:26,573 --> 00:32:28,402
Thank you.

487
00:32:29,293 --> 00:32:32,442
Can I hire an English tutor for you?

488
00:32:34,093 --> 00:32:36,344
So that when we go to events or parties,

489
00:32:36,344 --> 00:32:38,738
and my friends from overseas
come to visit us,

490
00:32:38,738 --> 00:32:40,680
you wouldn't be bored.

491
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:42,042
What do you think?

492
00:32:42,042 --> 00:32:45,553
Actually, I understand what they say.

493
00:32:45,553 --> 00:32:50,242
But I didn't respond because
I wasn't a part of your conversation.

494
00:32:50,242 --> 00:32:52,586
If they asked me, I would respond to them.

495
00:32:52,586 --> 00:32:53,989
I'm not bored.

496
00:32:53,989 --> 00:32:56,186
Are you sure?

497
00:32:56,186 --> 00:32:58,213
Sure.

498
00:32:58,213 --> 00:33:03,274
In the future,
I will talk to you in English, okay?

499
00:33:03,274 --> 00:33:04,928
Got it.

500
00:33:04,928 --> 00:33:07,042
Okay, let's go.

501
00:33:09,306 --> 00:33:11,722
Take her back to her place, okay?

502
00:33:14,602 --> 00:33:16,803
- Let me know when you get home.
- Okay.

503
00:33:39,082 --> 00:33:42,581
How was it?

504
00:33:42,581 --> 00:33:45,818
Gosh! I want to scream!

505
00:33:45,818 --> 00:33:47,922
I want to fly to outer space.

506
00:33:48,688 --> 00:33:50,489
It's the Queen?

507
00:33:51,776 --> 00:33:54,277
Both the Queen and that bitch Pie,
they introduced a new character.

508
00:33:54,277 --> 00:33:56,052
When she appeared,
they pushed me to the ground.

509
00:33:56,052 --> 00:33:58,325
- Who?
- Nicole from Boston.

510
00:33:58,325 --> 00:33:59,880
Mr. Supoj's daughter or something.

511
00:33:59,880 --> 00:34:02,419
She arrived and gave him the flowers.

512
00:34:02,419 --> 00:34:03,614
And they kept talking.

513
00:34:03,614 --> 00:34:06,130
They didn't stop talking.
If I said something out of the blue,

514
00:34:06,130 --> 00:34:08,722
I would look stupid!

515
00:34:09,600 --> 00:34:11,962
You poor thing.

516
00:34:11,962 --> 00:34:13,222
Hey.

517
00:34:14,146 --> 00:34:16,800
I've got good news to console you.

518
00:34:16,800 --> 00:34:18,322
- What?
- Well...

519
00:34:18,322 --> 00:34:20,842
I'm not sure if it's good news for you.

520
00:34:22,237 --> 00:34:26,576
The producer called and said
that the director wanted to see you.

